STORAGE  sledders.storage
  get(key, default?) -> Any
  set(key, value) -> bool
  delete(key) -> bool
  save() -> bool

  Storage supports nil, strings, finite numbers, booleans, vectors/colors and
  plain tables. Arrays must be contiguous 1-based integer arrays; object tables
  use string keys. Cycles and oversized/pathological tables are rejected.

LOG  sledders.log
  info(...)
  warn(...)
  error(...)

VALUES
  sledders.vector3(x,y,z) -> Vector3
  sledders.color(r,g,b,a?) -> Color
  Colors accept normalized 0..1 or byte-like >1 values and are normalized.

PROPERTY BAG
  isValid() -> bool
  keys() -> Array<String>
  isWritable(key) -> bool|nil
  get(key) -> Any
  set(key,value) -> bool

DEV  sledders.dev
  Requires both manifest permission "dev" and runtime config EnableDevApi=true.
  type(nameOrQuery) -> Type|nil
  types(query,max?) -> Array<Type>
  objects(query,max?) -> Array<Object>

TYPE
  name, fullName, assembly
  members(filter?,max?) -> Array<String>
  get(member) -> Any
  set(member,value) -> bool
  call(method,...) -> Any

OBJECT
  isValid() -> bool
  typeName() -> String
